## {{lb|en|naval slang|countable}} A [[service#Noun|service]] [[certificate#Noun|certificate]].
##* {{quote-book|en|date=13 August 1964|author=[[w:John Spicer (Australian politician)|John [Armstrong] Spicer]], Commissioner|chapter=Officers Principally Concerned|title=Report of Royal Commissioner on Loss of [[w:HMAS Voyager (D04)|H.M.A.S. “Voyager”]]|series=Papers Presented to [[w:Parliament of Australia|Parliament]]|seriesvolume=XIII|location=Canberra, A.C.T|publisher=[F]or the [[w:Australian Government|Government of the Commonwealth of Australia]] by A. J. Arthur, Commonwealth Government printer|page=3|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=uc1.c2647486&seq=307|oclc=221527156|passage=A perusal of the comments of officers under whom he {{quote-gloss|Captain Duncan Herbert Stevens}} has served as recorded in his “'''flimsies'''" indicates that he has almost consistently received high commendation for his service.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=John Wells|chapter=The Community of the Mid-Victorian Navy|title=The Royal Navy: An Illustrated Social History 1870–1982|location=Stroud, Gloucestershire&#59; Dover, N.H.|publisher=[[w:Alan Sutton|Alan Sutton Publishing]] in association with the [[w:National Museum of the Royal Navy, Portsmouth|Royal Naval Museum, Portsmouth]]|page=7|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/royalnavyillustr0000well/page/7/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-7509-0524-4|passage=Regulations required a commanding officer to render annual confidential reports on the character and ability of his officers&nbsp;– with particular reference to sobriety&nbsp;– on forms known as ‘'''flimsies'''’.}}
